Package: cybroid-edition-developer
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: CybroidOS maintainers <citos@cybroid.com>
Homepage: https://cybroid.com/cybroidos
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Depends: cybroid-plasma (>= @VERSION@), git, git-lfs, gh, build-essential, gdb, clang, cmake, make, ninja-build, meson, pkg-config, valgrind, strace, shellcheck, python3-venv, python3-pip, python3-dev, pipx, golang, rustc, cargo, nodejs, npm, default-jdk, maven, php-cli, composer, sqlite3, postgresql-client, mariadb-client, redis-tools, jq, vim, tmux, ripgrep, docker-ce, docker-ce-cli, containerd.io, docker-buildx-plugin, docker-compose-plugin
Recommends: code
Description: CybroidOS Developer: for engineers who build software
 The tools the industry works with: Visual Studio Code (from Microsoft's
 own repository); Docker Engine with Buildx and Compose (from Docker); Git
 with Git LFS and the GitHub CLI; GCC and Clang with CMake, Meson, Ninja,
 GDB, Valgrind and strace; Python, Go, Rust, Node.js, Java (OpenJDK 21 and
 Maven) and PHP (with Composer); PostgreSQL, MariaDB, Redis and SQLite
 clients; Postman for APIs and DBeaver for databases; Vim, tmux, ripgrep
 and jq.
 .
 The same CybroidOS as every edition (look, updates, Hangar), with these
 tools added. Chosen in the welcome at first sign-in, or later in Settings
 (any number of editions together), and installed from deb.cybroid.com.
